msgid ""
"5. Work with Qiskit Runtime options {#5-work-with-qiskit-runtime-options}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Error mitigation techniques allow users to mitigate circuit errors by "
"modeling the device noise at the time of execution. This typically results "
"in quantum pre-processing overhead related to model training, and classical "
"post-processing overhead to mitigate errors in the raw results by using the "
"generated model.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The error mitigation techniques built in to primitives are advanced resilience options. To specify these options, use the `resilience_level` option when submitting your job.\n"
"Sampler V2 does not support specifying resilience levels. However, you can turn on or off individual error mitigation / suppression methods.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following examples demonstrate the default options for dynamical "
"decoupling and twirling. Find more options and further details in the [Error"
" mitigation and suppression techniques](/guides/error-mitigation-and-"
"suppression-techniques) topic.\n"
msgstr ""

